lax fork patch for ReflowTeX — keep markers; sanitize SVG; injectable dvisvgm.

SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
Derived from: https://github.com/radek-p/reflowtex @ 36f8365eed25ece1db38e0059bcbba3c250802e1
              (src/encode/transforms.py, AGPL-3.0-or-later)

Three changes: (1) 'marker' joins SUPPORTED_NODE_TYPES — the patched schema
encodes it, and stripping it would silently unmoor every passage card;
(2) convert_pictures passes every converted picture through sanitize_svg,
an element/attribute allowlist (drawing primitives, structure, text,
transforms, clips, gradients survive; scripts, event handlers, style
sheets, foreign objects, and non-fragment references are dropped and
reported) — under -shell-escape a paper can emit arbitrary SVG through
dvisvgm-raw specials, and CSP on the serving side is defense in depth,
not the only wall; (3) the dvisvgm invocation is injectable per call
(REFLOWTEX_DVISVGM) so the trusted path can route conversion through the
pinned TeX container instead of assuming a host binary.

